            {
              "id": "u1-p24-05",
              "number": 5,
              "book_page": 44,
              "topic_id": "u1-rank-echelon",
              "r25_scope": "core",
              "question": "Determine the values of \\(p\\) such that the rank of \\(A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&1&-1&0\\\\4&4&-3&1\\\\p&2&2&2\\\\9&9&p&3\\end{bmatrix}\\) is 3.",
              "question_source_refs": [
                "TB-P0044"
              ],
              "answer_source_refs": [
                "TB-P1380"
              ],
              "answer": {
                "paragraphs": [
                  "For a \\(4\\times4\\) matrix to have rank \\(3\\), its determinant must be zero, but at least one third-order minor must be non-zero.",
                  "First compute the determinant:",
                  "\\[\\det A=-(p-2)(p+6).\\]",
                  "Therefore \\(\\det A=0\\) only when \\(p=2\\) or \\(p=-6\\).",
                  "Check that the rank does not fall below 3 for these values.",
                  "For \\(p=2\\), the third-order minor formed by rows \\(1,2,3\\) and columns \\(1,3,4\\) is",
                  "\\[\\begin{vmatrix}1&-1&0\\\\4&-3&1\\\\2&2&2\\end{vmatrix}=-2\\ne0.\\]",
                  "Hence for \\(p=2\\), rank \\(\\ge3\\); since \\(\\det A=0\\), rank \\(\\le3\\). Thus rank \\(=3\\).",
                  "For \\(p=-6\\), the third-order minor formed by rows \\(1,2,3\\) and columns \\(1,2,3\\) is",
                  "\\[\\begin{vmatrix}1&1&-1\\\\4&4&-3\\\\-6&2&2\\end{vmatrix}=-8\\ne0.\\]",
                  "Hence for \\(p=-6\\), rank \\(\\ge3\\); and again \\(\\det A=0\\), so rank \\(=3\\)."
                ],
                "result": "\\(p=2\\) or \\(p=-6\\).",
                "book_check": "Printed appendix answer: “No value of \\(p\\) is possible.”",
                "note": "Source discrepancy: direct calculation from the printed matrix gives \\(\\det A=-(p-2)(p+6)\\), and the displayed third-order minors are non-zero at \\(p=2\\) and \\(p=-6\\). Thus the supplied appendix answer is inconsistent with the printed question."
              }
